		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=5218&amp;p=37726#p37726"><![CDATA[
Build quality and reliability of the TYT radios is generally OK, with IIRC hardly anyone on the forum saying that they had a PA failure.<br>Build quality / factory QA testing on the Baofeng radios seems to be a bit lower.<br><br>Unfortunately both TYT and Baofeng continue to use a  quite old $1 FM transceiver chip in their handhelds, which suffers from desense and other problems.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Wed Jul 16, 2025 8:52 pm</p><hr />
